        {
          "clue": "t1.r1.h2",
          "kind": "herring",
          "holder": "dario",
          "text": "Worth writing down why the row hash is the right level for this. Keying on the row means resume and cache lookup need nothing but the dataset itself, no prompt callable, no live LLM object, so I can rebuild the whole hit/miss picture from the metadata DB on a cold process. That is exactly what cache_stats needs to be cheap. If the key depended on anything we can only compute by constructing the LLM, cache_stats stops being a thing you can call before a run and becomes another run.",
